course: dictionary
lesson: 2629
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word desk has two main ones, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. «Lily found it under a desk and gave it back to him without reading a word.» You can be under a piece of furniture, so here a desk is a table you sit at.
explain: Now read this: «If you are lost, stay inside the place, at a counter or desk where people work, and don't leave with anyone.» Here people work at the desk to help you, so a desk can also be a counter where you get help.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is someone sitting to read, write or work, or is someone asking for help? Then try that meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A desk is a table where you sit to read, write or work, often with drawers.
fact: A desk can also be a counter where you get help, like the front desk of a hotel.
fact: «Desk» is a noun. Its plural is «desks».
fact: «The teacher's desk» means the desk of one teacher. The apostrophe shows who owns it.
fact: In an earthquake drill, you drop, cover under a desk and hold on, because falling objects cause most injuries.
exercise: «Imagine your friend knocks a vase off the teacher's desk, and the teacher asks the class who did it.» Here, what is the desk? | A counter where you go to get help | A bus stop | *A table where the teacher sits and works | A kind of wooden bowl
exercise: A classroom has 5 rows of desks, with 4 desks in each row. How many desks are there in total? | 54 | *20 | 45 | 9
exercise: «If you are lost, stay inside the place, at a counter or desk where people work.» Where could you go to ask for help at a hotel? | The bathroom | *The front desk | The roof | The swimming pool
test: In «the teacher's desk», what does the apostrophe show? | *That the desk belongs to one teacher | That the desk is broken | That there are two teachers | That the word is a question
test: What is the plural of desk? | *desks | desky | desk's | deskes
exam: In «Lily found it under a desk», what does desk mean? | *A piece of furniture you can be under | A school subject | A counter where you get help | A type of bird
